data_case_b_plus_atom
#
# Case B+: Lys78 has TWO independent two-state choices at the SAME residue -- a backbone
# 'loop' choice (atoms N,CA,C,O,H) and a side-chain 'rotamer' choice (CB,CG,CD,CE,NZ).
# Both reuse the altloc letters A/B on residue 78, so the networks are separated by
# label_atom_id, not by residue. The residue sits in a short grey poly-ALA chain; the
# loop alternate tilts the peptide unit (CA fixed), the rotamer alternate swings chi1.
#
